{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1794532376, "title": "design/pricing-page \u00b7 not-ambitious run 1", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "theme": {"fg": "#d8dee9", "bg": "#1e1f1c", "palette": "#272822:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f8f8f2:#75715e:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f9f8f5"}}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Design a pricing page for an invoicing app for freelancers, as a single web page\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.172, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/pricing.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.845, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I built the pricing page as one self-contained HTML file with no dependencies: `<workspace>/pricing.html`. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  haven't opened it in a browser, so the layout and the billing toggle are untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What's on the page**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Hero and billing toggle:** a headline and a Monthly/Annual switch. Choosing Annual updates the prices\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and the \"billed\" text, and the annual option is labelled \"2 months free\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Three plans:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Starter** is free: 3 clients, 5 invoices a month.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Freelancer** costs $12 a month ($10 on the annual plan). It's highlighted as \"Most popular\" and has\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  unlimited invoices, reminders, recurring invoices and multi-currency.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Studio** costs $29 a month ($24 on the annual plan). It adds a team, a client portal, reports and an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  API.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reassurance:** a line under the plans says payment processing fees are charged by the processor, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  nothing added on top. A trust strip below lists \"Cancel anytime\", \"No per-invoice fees\" and similar.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Comparison table:** it groups features by invoicing, getting paid, work and team, and support. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  scrolls sideways on small screens.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Testimonial, FAQ and closing sign-up button:** the FAQ covers the free-trial card, plan limits,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  cancelling, fees, discounts and refunds.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Design choices**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A calm green and cream palette, with a dark theme that follows the system setting.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - On mobile the plans stack, with the featured plan first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The toggle is keyboard-accessible, there are visible focus outlines, and animations switch off for people\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  who prefer reduced motion.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The product name (Quillbill), the prices, the plan limits, the testimonial and the discount and refund terms\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  are all placeholders I made up. Replace them with your real details. To preview the page, run `open\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"<workspace>/pricing.html\"`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.591, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[119.036, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/pricing.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[128.232, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I rewrote `<workspace>/pricing.html` with a lot more in it. I haven't opened it in a browser, so the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  animations, the calculator and the layout are untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **New**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Hero invoice:** a tilted mock invoice whose \"PAID\" stamp slams down a moment after load. It shows the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  product's payoff right at the top of the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Currency switcher (USD, EUR, GBP):** prices and the yearly totals update with it. The numbers also count\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  up when you flip monthly/annual.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **\"Does it pay for itself?\" calculator:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Inputs:** two sliders, for invoices per month and your hourly rate.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Output:** it shows the monthly value of admin time you'd get back, and highlights the plan that fits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Starter case:** at 5 invoices a month or fewer, it says Starter covers you.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Paid case:** above that, it says how many times Freelancer would pay for itself.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Assumptions:** it assumes about 20 minutes of admin per invoice by hand versus 3 with the app, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page says so.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stats strip:** the numbers count up as it scrolls into view.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Comparison table:** the Freelancer column is tinted so it stands out.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Polish:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Background:** a soft gradient glow behind the hero.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Plan cards:** they lift on hover.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Sections:** each fades in on scroll.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Mobile:** a sticky \"Start free trial\" bar appears once the plans scroll off screen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Reduced motion:** every animation turns off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Placeholders to replace**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The usage stats (48,000+ freelancers, $2.1B invoiced, 9 days faster) are made up. I put an \"illustrative\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  figures\" footnote at the bottom, which you should remove once the numbers are real.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The EUR and GBP prices are hand-picked round numbers, not converted rates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Everything from the first version is still a placeholder: the Quillbill name, the plan limits, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  testimonial and the discount and refund terms.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Next I could add a plan-finder quiz, a \"Contact sales\" tier for agencies, or a version split into components\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for a real codebase. Tell me which you want.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
